ail(\"unread\") together.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user asks: \"What needs my attention across my mailboxes this week?\" — turn sent at 2026-10-10T16:49:48.996Z UTC.\n\n\"This week\" — resolve relative to sent-at 2026-10-10 (Saturday? Let''s check: 2026-10-10. Oct 10 2026 is a Saturday.) This week would be Mon Oct 5 – Sun Oct 11, 2026.\n\nI need to get an overview across all mailboxes. Use aggregateInbox. But perMailbox default 8. The user asks what needs attention this week — so I want recent emails. aggregateInbox gives most recent inbox emails merged. It doesn''t take a time window though. Let me call aggregateInbox with a decent perMailbox, maybe 20, to see this week''s mail.\n\nLet me call aggregateInbox with perMailbox 20.\n\nAlso maybe searchMail for recent unread / flagged. But let''s start with aggregateInbox.\n\nLet me do aggregateInbox perMailbox=20. Maybe also a searchMail for \"is:unread\" — but the search query language unknown. Let''s just use aggregateInbox first, and possibly aggregateInbox in parallel with searchMail for \"unread\" and \"urgent\". Let''s issue aggregateInbox and searchMail calls in parallel.\n\nI''ll do: aggregateInbox(perMailbox=20), searchMail(\"unread\", null), searchMail(\"urgent\", null). Hmm, searchMail queries might be keyword-based. Let''s do a couple.\n\nActually let''s be careful not to over-call. I''ll issue aggregateInbox(20) plus searchMail(\"reply requested\", null)? Eh. Let''s start with aggregateInbox(20) alone and decide.\n\nActually the guidance says issue searches together. But the key data source is aggregateInbox. Let me do aggregateInbox with 20 and searchMail for \"unread\" to catch flagged items.\n\nLet me just do aggregateInbox first — its result will inform. But time/turns cost. I''ll do aggregateInbox(20) and searchMail(\"unread\") together."}],"createdAt":1792940793004},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"mailboxes":1,"count":20,"emails":[{"mailboxId":"4c