INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('d42785bc-f1c3-4c51-b7d0-0e97ba110bbd','1679f354-ecd2-43af-a1b0-44c15cdb3ddf','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The user is asking if the \"brief\" mentions the same deadline as the \"kickoff email.\"\n\n1.  **Recall/Locate the kickoff email:** The previous turns established the \"Rebrand kickoff email\" from Raj Mehta (ana@harness.test).\n    *   Email subject: \"Rebrand kickoff\"\n    *   Content related to deadline: \"We agreed to start the rebrand on **October 5**.\" (The delivery of the moodboard was due by Friday, Sep 25, which was related to the kickoff.) The core start date is Oct 5.\n2.  **Recall/Locate the brief:** The previous turns established the content of `brief.txt`.\n    *   Brief content: \"Rebrand brief\\nKickoff: 2026-10-05\\nReview: 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC\\n\"\n3.  **Compare:**\n    *   Email mentions a start/agreed date of \"October 5.\"\n    *   Brief mentions a \"Kickoff\" date of \"2026-10-05.\"\n4.  **Confirm the finding and answer the user.**The user is asking if the \"brief\" mentions the same deadline as the \"kickoff email.\"\n1.  **Identify the kickoff email deadline:**\n    *   Looking back, the kickoff email from Raj (Sep 21, 2026) asked Ana to \"send me the moodboard by Friday\".\n    *   The user''s follow-up in the previous turn noted that the Friday in question (relative to the Sep 21 email) was Sep 25.\n    *   The deadline from the email is the delivery of the moodboard by Friday (Sep 25).\n2.  **Identify the brief contents/deadlines:**\n    *   The brief contents are: \"Rebrand brief / Kickoff: 2026-10-05 / Review: 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC\".\n    *   The brief does *not* mention \"Friday, Sep 25\" or the delivery of a \"moodboard.\" It only mentions the Kickoff and the Review date.\n3.  **Compare:**\n    *   Email deadline (moodboard submission): Sep 25.\n    *   Brief deadlines (Kickoff/Review): Oct 5 / Oct 8.\n    *   They are different.\n\nI have all the information needed. I don''t need to call any tools.The user isThe user asks: \"Does the brief mention the same deadline as the kickoff email?\"\n\nKickoff email (from Raj, Sep 21): \"Can you send me the moodboard by Friday\" — sent Mon Sep 21, 2026. Friday = Sep 25, 2026. And \"confirm whether Bo can join the first review.\"\n\nBrief: \"Kickoff: 2026-10-05 / Review: 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC\". No mention of \"Friday\" or Sep 25 moodboard deadline. It mentions kickoff Oct 5 and review Oct 8 15:00.\n\nSo answer: No. The brief has no deadline at all — only a kickoff date (Oct 5) and a review date/time (Oct 8 15:00). The email''s only deadline is \"moodboard by Friday\" = Fri Sep 25, 2026. Neither date in the brief matches Sep 25.\n\nAlso worth noting the review date Oct 8 15:00 matches the calendar invite \"Rebrand review\" — but the calendar query \"rebrand\" returned 0 events, which I should flag carefully. Earlier I asserted the Oct 8 invite existed. In this conversation''s tool results, listEvents with query \"rebrand\" returned count 0. But in the earlier turn (per my own reply) I referenced \"Rebrand review Thu Oct 8 15:00–15:45 UTC\". Hmm — that came from a prior turn''s context I claimed. In this actual tool history, the only listEvents call returned 0 events for \"rebrand\". So I shouldn''t assert the calendar invite''s existence strongly. Actually my previous message claimed the Oct 8 invite. But the tool said 0 events matching \"rebrand\". That''s a contradiction I should correct honestly now? The user''s question is about deadline comparison. I should be accurate.\n\nLet me verify the calendar now to be sure — a listEvents over Oct 5–9 without query would reveal the \"Rebrand review\". That''s worth one call to substantiate or correct. Also the earlier claim that \"Rebrand review\" event exists. Let me check the window 2026-10-01 to 2026-10-10 across calendars. Then answer.\n\nAlso should I verify the \"Friday\" deadline interpretation? Email sent Mon 21 Sep 2026 — is 21 Sep 2026 a Monday? Let''s compute: Jan 1 2026 is a Thursday. Doomsday 2026: doomsday for 2026 — 2026 = 2000 + 26; anchor for 2000s is Tuesday. 26/12 = 2 remainder 2; 2/4 = 0; 2+2+0 = 4; Tuesday + 4 = Saturday. So doomsday 2026 = Saturday. Doomsday dates: 3/14? No — doomsday dates: 2/28 (2026 not leap), 4/4, 6/6, 8/8, 10/10, 12/12, 5/9, 9/5, 7/11, 11/7, 3/14. So 9/5/2026 is Saturday. Then 9/19 Saturday, so 9/21 = Monday. Yes, 21 Sep 2026 is Monday. Friday = 25 Sep 2026. Good, consistent with my prior message.\n\nSo the brief does not mention the moodboard deadline at all. Also brief''s \"Review: 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC\" vs email \"first review\" (no date given in email).\n\nLet me do the calendar check to be solid about the Oct 8 event.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user is asking if the \"brief\" mentions the same deadline as the \"kickoff email.\"\n\n1.  **Recall/Locate the kickoff email:** The previous turns established the \"Rebrand kickoff email\" from Raj Mehta (ana@harness.test).\n    *   Email subject: \"Rebrand kickoff\"\n    *   Content related to deadline: \"We agreed to start the rebrand on **October 5**.\" (The delivery of the moodboard was due by Friday, Sep 25, which was related to the kickoff.) The core start date is Oct 5.\n2.  **Recall/Locate the brief:** The previous turns established the content of `brief.txt`.\n    *   Brief content: \"Rebrand brief\\nKickoff: 2026-10-05\\nReview: 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC\\n\"\n3.  **Compare:**\n    *   Email mentions a start/agreed date of \"October 5.\"\n    *   Brief mentions a \"Kickoff\" date of \"2026-10-05.\"\n4.  **Confirm the finding and answer the user.**The user is asking if the \"brief\" mentions the same deadline as the \"kickoff email.\"\n1.  **Identify the kickoff email deadline:**\n    *   Looking back, the kickoff email from Raj (Sep 21, 2026) asked Ana to \"send me the moodboard by Friday\".\n    *   The user''s follow-up in the 