:00 UTC\" from the brief.\n4.  **Conclusion:** The brief does not mention the same deadline. The email deadline is Sep 25 (moodboard), and the brief''s deadlines are Oct 5 and Oct 8 (kickoff/review).\n\nI will state clearly that they are different and identify both sets of dates for clarity.The user is asking if the \"brief\" mentions the same deadline as the \"kickoff email.\"\n\nI have previously established the following:\n1.  **Kickoff email deadline:** The email sent on Sep 21, 2026, mentioned sending the moodboard by \"Friday,\" which is Sep 25, 2026.\n2.  **Brief content:** `brief.txt` contains: \"Rebrand brief / Kickoff: 2026-10-05 / Review: 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC\". The brief has no deadline matching Sep 25.\n3.  **Calendar events (rebrand):** I searched for events across all calendars between Oct 1 and Oct 12, 2026. I found a \"Design review\" event on `Work` calendar for Oct 8, 2026, from 15:00:00 to 16:00:00 UTC. This matches the time/date of the \"Review\" line in the brief (2026-10-08 15:00 UTC).\n\n**Comparison:**\n*   Email deadline: Sep 25, 2026.\n*   Brief content (dates): Kickoff Oct 5, Review Oct 8.\n\nThe brief does not mention the Sep 25 deadline from the email. However, the brief''s Review date (OctThe calendar event on Oct 8 15:00–16:00 is titled \"Design review\" in the Work calendar, not \"Rebrand review\". So my earlier claim of a \"Rebrand review\" event was wrong — I should correct that. The brief''s \"Review: 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC\" aligns with the \"Design review\" event in the Work calendar (Studio 2), and the \"rebrand\" query returned 0 events, meaning no event has \"rebrand\" in its title/description.\n\nNow the actual question: Does the brief mention the same deadline as the kickoff email?\n\nKickoff email''s deadline: \"send me the moodboard by Friday\" — Friday 25 Sep 2026 (email sent Mon 21 Sep 2026). Note: this deadline is in the past relative to the message sent-at Oct 25 — the deadline has already passed. Hmm, interesting: the 