 email are consistent only in that the kickoff starts Oct 5; the brief drops the moodboard deadline entirely.","createdAt":1792940805833}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**No — they don''t share a deadline, and the dates don''t even overlap.**\n\n- **Kickoff email (Raj, Mon 21 Sep 2026):** one deadline — *\"send me the moodboard by Friday\"* → **Fri 25 Sep 2026**. Plus a second ask with no date: whether Bo joins the first review.\n- **Brief (`rebrand/brief.txt`):** no deadline at all. It has only **Kickoff 2026-10-05** (a start date) and **Review 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC**.\n- **No overlap:** 25 Sep appears nowhere in the brief, and \"moodboard\" appears nowhere in it either. The nearest anchor is the brief''s Oct 8, 15:00 UTC review slot — which lines up with the **\"Design review\"** event on the **Work** calendar (`ana@harness.test`, Studio 2, 15:00–16:00 UTC), not with the email''s Friday ask.\n\nTwo corrections to what I told you earlier, now that I''ve checked the calendar properly: there is **no event titled \"Rebrand review\"** — searching all three calendars for \"rebrand\" returned **0 events**, and the Oct 8 slot is titled \"Design review.\" I also shouldn''t have called the moodboard \"still open\" as if it were pending — **the Sep 25 deadline passed a month ago** (today being 25 Oct) with no reply in the thread. So the brief and the email are consistent only in that the kickoff starts Oct 5; the brief drops the moodboard deadline entirely."}','assistant','v2','2026-10-25T15:06:45.251Z','7f765568-8c0d-56ce-8b89-105126fefedf');
