INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('69abbfad-7e86-4446-ad54-c66fd3b8e73a','1679f354-ecd2-43af-a1b0-44c15cdb3ddf','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The user is asking if any of their orders have shipped recently.\nThis is a general question about external services (like shipping or e-commerce). I need to check my available tools to see if I can search for this type of information across the workspace.\n\nAvailable tools include:\n1. `listMailboxes`, `listCalendars`, `listDrives`, `search_tools` (which led to `searchFiles`, `findMemberFiles`, `moveFile`, `searchContacts`, `listEvents`).\n2. Mail reading/searching: `searchMail`, `aggregateInbox`.\n3. Drive searching: `searchFiles`.\n\nMy tools primarily deal with emails, calendars, and files in connected drives.\nI cannot check external order statuses directly.\nI can only check if there are emails *about* orders shipping.\n\nPlan:\n1. Use `aggregateInbox` or `searchMail` to look for common keywords related to shipping and orders in all connected mailboxes.\n2. List the mails found, focusing on recent ones.\n3. If none are found, state that I cannot find any shipping information.\n4. I will start by using `aggregateInbox` with relevant keywords.The user is asking if any of their orders shipped recently.\nI need to search for shipping/order related information in emails (inboxes/archives) or files (drives).\nA good starting point is to search the mailbox for keywords like \"ship,\" \"shipped,\" \"tracking,\" \"order,\" or \"delivery.\"\nSince this is a general request about personal activity, searching the aggregated inbox and all drives is appropriate.\n\nFirst, I will list the mailboxes and drives just in case they need clarification, although the prompt implies \"my\" orders (so it should be the user''s connected resources).\nI will prioritize searching for the relevant terms in the mail.\n\nPlan:\n1. Use `aggregateInbox` to search for recent shipping/order confirmation emails.\n2. Use `searchFiles` across all drives to look for order documents/invoices that might contain shipping info.\n\nInitial thought: Search mail first.\nKeywords: \"shipped\", \"order confirmation\", \"shipping update\", \"delivered\".\nTimeframe: \"Recently\" (I will define this as the last 30 days relative to the turn sent-at: 2026-10-25T14:14:13.354Z).\nSince I am not given a specific time range, I will search for the most relevant emails and rely on the tool to provide recent results, then filter by context.\n\nI will start by calling `aggregateInbox` and `searchFiles`.The user is asking if any of their orders shipped recently.\nI need to look through their mail or files for shipping updates. Since the request is general (\"any order\"), I should start by searching emails for relevant keywords.\nThe available tools are: `listMailboxes`, `aggregateInbox`, `searchMail`, `searchFiles`.\nI will search the inbox for keywords like \"ship\", \"shipped\", \"order\", \"tracking\".\n\nFirst, I''ll check the inbox for emails containing shipping updates.\nSecond, I''ll check drives for any files like \"invoice\", \"shipping confirmation\", \"tracking details\" if emails are sparse.\n\nPlan:\n1. Search `aggregateInbox` for terms like \"shipped\", \"order\", \"tracking\", \"ship\"`.\n2. If mail is insufficient, search drives for relevant files (less likely to be helpful for \"recently shipped\" status unless they are looking at a specific document).\n\nLet''s start with email.\nKeywords: \"shipped\", \"shipping\", \"order\", \"track\", \"delivered\".The user asks: \"Did any order of mine ship recently?\" This is a mail question — order/shipping notifications. I should search mail across all mailboxes for shipping/order confirmations.\n\nLet me search mail for \"shipped\", \"order\", \"tracking\", \"delivery\". And also aggregate inbox to see recent mail.\n\nLet me do parallel searches: searchMail \"shipped\" (mailboxId null), searchMail \"order\", and aggregateInbox maybe. Let''s do a couple.\n\nNote \"recently\" — relative to sent-at 2026-10-25T14:14Z. So maybe last week or so. I''ll look at what comes back and filter by date.\n\nLet me issue searchMail queries: \"shipped\", \"order\", \"tracking\", \"delivery\". Four calls in parallel plus aggregateInbox? aggregateInbox perMailbox 15. That''s fine.\n\nActually to be efficient: searchMail \"shipped\" OR \"order\" — the query is free text; I''ll do separate queries. Let me do 3-4 searches in parallel.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user is asking if any of their orders have shipped recently.\nThis is a general question about external services (like shipping or e-commerce). I need to check my available tools to see if I can search for this type of information across the workspace.\n\nAvailable tools include:\n1. `listMailboxes`, `listCalendars`, `listDrives`, `search_tools` (which led to `searchFiles`, `findMemberFiles`, `moveFile`, `searchContacts`, `listEvents`).\n2. Mail reading/searching: `searchMail`, `aggregateInbox`.\n3. Drive searching: `searchFiles`.\n\nMy tools primarily deal with emails, calendars, and files in connected drives.\nI cannot check external order statuses directly.\nI can only check if there are emails *about* orders shipping.\n\nPlan:\n1. Use `aggregateInbox` or `searchMail` to look for common keywords related to shipping and orders in all connected mailboxes.\n2. List the mails found, focusing on recent ones.\n3. If none are found, state that I cannot find any shipping information.\n4. I will start by using `aggregateInbox` with relevant keywords.The user is asking if any of their orders shipped recently.\nI need to search for shipping/order related information in emails (inboxes/archives) or files (drives).\nA good starting point is to search the mailbox for keywords like \"ship,\" \"shipped,\" \"tracking,\" \"order,\" or \"delivery.\"\nSince this is a general request about personal activity, searching the aggregated inbox and all drives is appropriate.\n\nFirst, I will list the mailboxes and drives just in case they need clarification, although the prompt implies \"my\" orders (so it should be the user''s connected resources).\nI will prioritize searching for the relevant terms in the mail.\n\nPlan:\n1. Use `aggregateInbox` to search for recent shipping/order confirmation emails.\n2. Use `searchFiles` across all drives to look for order documents/invoices that might contain shipping info.\n\nInitial thought: Search mail first.\nKeywords: \"shipped\", \"order confirmation\", \"shipping update\", \"delivered\".\nTimeframe: \"Recently\" (I will define this as the last 30 days relative to the turn sent-at: 2026-10-25T14:14:13.354Z).\nSince I am not given a specific time range, I will search for the most relevant emails and rely on the tool to provide recent results, then filter by context.\n\nI will start by calling `aggregateInbox` and `searchFiles`.The user is asking if any of their orders shipped recently.\nI need to look through their mail or files for shipping updates. Since the request is general (\"any order\"), I should start by searching emails for relevant keywords.\nThe available tools are: `listMailboxes`, `aggregateInbox`, `searchMail`, `searchFiles`.\nI will search the inbox for keywords like \"ship\", \"shipped\", \"order\", \"tracking\".\n\nFirst, I''ll check the inbox for emails containing shipping updates.\nSecond, I''ll check drives for any files like \"invoice\", \"shipping confirmation\", \"tracking details\" if emails are sparse.\n\nPlan:\n1. Search `aggregateInbox` for terms like \"shipped\", \"order\", \"tracking\", \"ship\"`.\n2. If mail is insufficient, search drives for relevant files (less likely to be helpful for \"recently shipped\" status unless they are looking at a specific document).\n\nLet''s start with email.\nKeywords: \"shipped\", \"shipping\", \"order\", \"track\", \"delivered\".The user asks: \"Did any order of mine ship recent