ipment\"}` -> Found many unrelated emails from \"Edge Sender\".\n3. `searchMail{mailboxId:null,query:\"A-42\"}` -> Found the same \"Your order A-42 has shipped\" email.\n4. `listMailboxes{}` -> Confirmed `ana@harness.test` is the mailbox.\n\nI need to check the thread containing the \"Your order A-42 has shipped\" email (`WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDI4MV0`) for tracking numbers or updates. Since I don''t have the thread ID readily available in the snippet but I have the email ID, I can search for emails from \"Acme Store\" specifically regarding tracking.\n\nLet''s refine the search. I will search for \"Acme Store\" again, maybe looking for keywords like \"tracking\", \"shipping\", \"delivery\".\nSince I know the user is asking about order A-42, I will also search for that combination.\nI''ll search all mailboxes for \"Acme Store tracking\" and \"Awaiting for results.\nSince I only have one mailbox, I could search there, but the query applies to all connected mailboxes anyway.The user is asking about the tracking situation for \"it\", which refers to the order mentioned in the previous turn''s email search (\"Your order A-42 has shipped\" from \"Acme Store\").\n\nFrom the previous search results:\n1.  There is an email: `\"Your order A-42 has shipped\"` from `\"Acme Store\"` with `id: WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDI4MV0`.\n2.  The snippet is empty, so I need to read the email body to find the tracking details.\n\nPlan:\n1.  Find the email ID: `WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDI4MV0`.\n2.  Read the email body using `readEmailBody`.\n3.  If the body contains tracking information, present it. If not, inform the user.\n4.  I don''t need to check drives for tracking, as the previous request was only about the \"brief for the rebrand,\" and this is a follow-up on a specific email/order.\n\nTools to use: `readEmailBody`\nArguments: `emailId=\"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDI4MV0\"`\nMailbox: `ana@harness.test` (derived from the previous context/search result).The user is asking about the \"tracking situati