eed to search across all mailboxes using keywords and phrases that typically denote newsletters or digests.\nI will use `searchMail` with various queries.\nKeywords: \"newsletter\", \"digest\", \"daily update\", \"weekly roundup\", \"summary\", \"subscription\".\n\nQueries:\n1. `subject:(\"newsletter\" OR \"digest\" OR \"daily update\" OR \"weekly roundup\" OR \"summary\")`\n2. `from:(\\\"newsletter\\\" OR \\\"digest\\\" OR \\\"subscription\\\")`\n3. `subject:*digest*`\n4. `subject:*newsletter*`\n5. `snippet:digest`\n6. `snippet:newsletter`\nI will execute these queries using `searchMail` across all mailboxes (since `mailboxId` is null).The user asks to find emails that look like newsletters or digests. I should search mail across all mailboxes for newsletter-ish terms. Let me search \"newsletter\", \"digest\", \"weekly\", \"unsubscribe\".\n\nSearch results for \"shipped order tracking\" returned 0 earlier — odd, but maybe search is phrase-based. So I should use likely literal words. \"Shop Weekly\" exists in inbox — \"This week at the shop\" from \"Shop Weekly\" looks like a newsletter/digest. Also \"Edge Sender\" bulk test emails maybe not newsletters.\n\nLet me do parallel searches: \"newsletter\", \"digest\", \"weekly\", \"unsubscribe\".\n\nAlso I could scan listEmails inbox pages for senders like newsletters. But search first."}],"createdAt":1792940824600},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":1,"emails":[{"mailboxId":"4c045289-9c42-53f9-a3d7-2dfac727d3d0","mailbox":"ana@harness.test","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDI4NF0","threadId":"<e2e-privacy-vectors-0001@harness.test>","from":"Shop Weekly","subject":"This week at the shop","date":"Sat Sep 26 2026 08:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""}]},"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-91e770195a6c9e68","toolName":"searchMail","args":{"query":"newsletter","mailboxId":null}},"updatedAt":1792940828144},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvoc