apply `newsletter` to the Shop Weekly message?","createdAt":1792940828259}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**One candidate — and it''s a test fixture, not a real newsletter.**\n\n## ana@harness.test\n\n- **Shop Weekly** — *This week at the shop* — Sat 26 Sep 2026, 08:00 UTC. The only mail matching \"newsletter\", \"weekly\" or \"unsubscribe\". But its body is a privacy/tracking test harness message: it lists pixel URLs, blocked-image modes, tracking-parameter links and a SendGrid click-tracked link, ending \"Bottom of the message.\" It''s built to *look* like a digest; there''s no actual shop content in it.\n\nNothing else qualifies:\n\n- **\"digest\"** — zero results anywhere.\n- The remaining inbox traffic is transactional (Acme Store shipment, Harness Bank debit, GitHub OTP), personal (Raj Mehta), or edge-case fixtures from \"Edge Sender\" (JSON-LD, hostile HTML, attachment tests).\n- No mail has the `newsletter` or `promotional` label applied.\n\nIf you expected real subscriptions — a news briefing, product digest, industry roundup — none are arriving in this mailbox at all. Want me to set up a workflow that labels genuine newsletters as they arrive, or apply `newsletter` to the Shop Weekly message?"}','assistant','v2','2026-10-25T15:07:04.600Z','7f765568-8c0d-56ce-8b89-105126fefedf');
