INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('469f91db-ae26-4d87-a6da-b87572a43e80','1679f354-ecd2-43af-a1b0-44c15cdb3ddf','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Thinking Process:\n\n1.  **Analyze the Request:** The user is asking if all seven connected drives contain the \"same files in them.\"\n2.  **Identify Necessary Tools/Actions:** To answer this, I need to inspect the contents of each drive. The `listDrives` output provided the `driveId` for all 7 drives. The tool `listDrives` can only list the drives; I need a mechanism to list *files* within them. The available tool for files is `search_files` or implicitly `list_files` (which is often synonymous with browsing a drive). Since the prompt allows me to \"browse a folder\" and \"search every drive by name or content,\" the logical next step is to attempt to list the root contents or perform a general search across all of them.\n3.  **Determine the Scope:** I have 7 drive IDs:\n    *   `c92b4299-1f7c-571a-ab7e-aa39d6c8bb32` (SFTP)\n    *   `66e47377-dba1-5bfd-945e-a2e575ae1511` (FTP)\n    *   `7966bf69-d3ed-5a47-9bd7-9a807d9a645d` (FTP - Scoped)\n    *   `6b8c0a7c-3d05-5f0c-b50c-e3da0da47f2b` (FTP)\n    *   `1a17bf00-c9d1-5cdd-81d1-ce8b6583982c` (WebDAV)\n    *   `4258fe0c-92ff-5c5b-85dd-797a798ab5c6` (S3)\n    *   `a8caddaf-15c9-57c2-a67e-93e7cffc3beb` (S3)\n4.  **Formulate the Plan:** I need to list the contents of the root directory (or perform a general file listing/search) for *every* drive ID. Since I don''t have a direct `list_root_files(driveId)` tool, I will use `search_files` with an empty query to see what is at the top level of each drive.\n5.  **Construct Tool Calls (Batch Execution):** I must execute these calls simultaneously to be efficient.\n\n    *   `search_files(driveId=''c92b4299-1f7c-571a-ab7e-aa39d6c8bb32'', query=''all'')`\n    *   `search_files(driveId=''66e47377-dba1-5bfd-945e-a2e575ae1511'', query=''all'')`\n 