ntents of all drives. This means listing the top-level contents of each drive. I should find the tool for listing drive contents. Let me search for \"list files in drive\" or \"browse drive folder\".\n\nThe user''s question: \"Do all of those drives have the same files in them?\" This is a comparison question across all 7 drives. I need to browse each drive''s top level.\n\nLet me search for the relevant tool."}],"createdAt":1792940828439},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"results":[{"name":"listFolder","description":"List the files and folders inside a folder of ONE specific drive. Omit folderId for the drive''s top level, then pass the fileId of a folder to go d...","score":21.47},{"name":"unpinFolder","description":"Remove one of your drive folder pins. The folder is untouched.","score":12.65},{"name":"createFolder","description":"Create a new folder in a drive, inside an existing folder or at the drive''s top level when parentFolderId is omitted.","score":11.8},{"name":"listPins","description":"List the drive folders you pinned for quick access in this workspace.","score":11.57},{"name":"pinFolder","description":"Pin a drive folder for quick access. The pin is yours alone; nobody else sees it.","score":11.52}],"loaded":["listFolder","unpinFolder","createFolder","listPins","pinFolder"],"message":"Found and loaded 5 tool(s): listFolder, unpinFolder, createFolder, listPins, pinFolder. They are available on your next turn — call them directly."},"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a89da0b4b3a71066","toolName":"search_tools","args":{"query":"list files in drive browse drive folder contents"}},"updatedAt":1792940828441},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1792940828442,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The user wants me to compare the contents of 7 different connected drives.\nI have the `listFolder` tool, which can list files and folders inside a drive.\nTo compare them, I 